# Lightroom 6.14 Map module: replace Google Maps with the mapfix shim (Leaflet, OpenStreetMap, Esri).
# No Google API key needed. See README section "mapfix shim".
#
# Apply this patch file to each of these three Lua files:
#   Windows: LOCATIONMAPVIEW.LUA, REVERSEGEOCODESERVICEFALLBACK.LUA, LOCATIONVIEWCONTROLLER.LUA
#   Mac:     LocationMapView.lua, ReverseGeocodeServiceFallback.lua, LocationViewController.lua
# e.g.  patchluastr.py LOCATIONMAPVIEW.LUA -p patches/mapfix-shim.patch -o LOCATIONMAPVIEW.bin
#
# Each file contains only some of the strings below, so "not found, nothing to patch"
# messages are expected. Every file must report at least one "Updated ... strings".
#
# Works on the original Adobe module and on modules patched for a Google API key.

# Map page and hidden reverse geocoding page: load the shim instead of Google's API.
# (Map page: the URL used with enablePremiereLicense = false in config.lua.)
< http://maps.google.com/maps/api/js?sensor=false
> https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/astuder/lightroom-map-fix@1/shim/mapfix-shim.js?sensor=false

# Map page: the URL used with a premiere license (Lightroom's default without config.lua).
< https://maps-api-ssl.google.com/maps/api/js?
> https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/astuder/lightroom-map-fix@1/shim/mapfix-shim.js?

# Map page, premiere URL: rename the hard-coded Google API version parameter, so that
# locationModule.api_version in config.lua is the only "v=" the shim sees.
< &sensor=false&v=
> &sensor=false&gv=

# Online check: Lightroom shows "Map is offline" if this URL can't be loaded. It checks the
# shim itself (same @1 release line as above), so Leaflet updates inside the shim never
# require patching again.
< https://maps.google.com/maps/api/js?sensor=false
> https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/astuder/lightroom-map-fix@1/shim/mapfix-shim.js
